# POS Supporting API Access

Anyone with POS access (`sales.view`, `sales.create`, or `sales.update`) must be able to use the supporting read/config APIs needed inside POS.

When changing RBAC, API guards, or POS data loading, keep POS users able to access:

- clients needed for sale/customer selection
- stock/products/services needed for item selection
- tax types and tax default settings needed for VAT/tax calculation
- payment accounts and payment methods needed for tendering
- chart of accounts income accounts used by POS item/account mapping
- tenant list/switch and onboarding status used by the POS shell/layout
- tenant logo/uploads displayed by the POS UI

Do not require broad dashboard/accounting/admin access for these POS support calls. Prefer adding `sales.view`, `sales.create`, or `sales.update` to the relevant API access rule when the endpoint is used by POS.

Also check route-level guards such as `requirePermission()` inside API handlers. If a POS-used endpoint has its own guard, it must also accept POS permissions (for example via `requireAnyPermission()`), otherwise middleware access will still end in `403`.
